From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:18:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Arachne: value-initialise WallToolPathsParams

Arachne::WallToolPathsParams has no default member initialisers. Fill/FillConcentric.cpp and
Fill/FillConcentricInternal.cpp declare it on the stack and set only some fields, so
min_length_factor and is_top_or_bottom_layer hold stack garbage. WallToolPaths::removeSmallLines
uses both to decide whether short odd lines are dropped, so tiny corner segments in narrow
internal solid regions appear or vanish depending on what the stack held. In Slicewright this
showed as G-code that differed with the calling thread (found by the R22 investigation: 17254,
17228 or 17202 moves for the same input; official OrcaSlicer v2.4.2 happens to read zeros).

Value-initialise all fields (zero / false). Zero reproduces the official v2.4.2 CLI output.
Upstream main has since added default initialisers as well (with min_length_factor = 0.5f, which
changes the output; this patch keeps the v2.4.2 behaviour).

Purpose: Fix uninitialised stack members that made G-code depend on stack garbage (min_length_factor, is_top_or_bottom_layer).
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: Backport (modified)
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Arachne/WallToolPaths.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Arachne/WallToolPaths.hpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Arachne/WallToolPaths.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Arachne/WallToolPaths.hpp
@@ -23,14 +23,14 @@
 class WallToolPathsParams
 {
 public:
-    float   min_bead_width;
-    float   min_feature_size;
-    float   min_length_factor;
-    float   wall_transition_length;
-    float   wall_transition_angle;
-    float   wall_transition_filter_deviation;
-    int     wall_distribution_count;
-    bool    is_top_or_bottom_layer;
+    float   min_bead_width{0.f};
+    float   min_feature_size{0.f};
+    float   min_length_factor{0.f};
+    float   wall_transition_length{0.f};
+    float   wall_transition_angle{0.f};
+    float   wall_transition_filter_deviation{0.f};
+    int     wall_distribution_count{0};
+    bool    is_top_or_bottom_layer{false};
 
     coord_t wall_maximum_resolution = meshfix_maximum_resolution();
     coord_t wall_maximum_deviation  = meshfix_maximum_deviation();
